        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/ba8739/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2021-10-14T03:49:40.530Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Minted by reducing WM to 0, with heroes still in the teens. Once he got to the flip side I had good setup, and he revealed Unwise Wager which was very easy to flip back. Closest I came to losing was 1 card in Luminary’s deck, but turning “Citizen Dusk” back down on her face got rid of that threat. It was a combo beatdown by Rhinolope Naturalist and the roguishly handsome and strong Ansel that spelled the end of the Great Blue Annoyance when he didn’t have his -2 DR anymore.</p>",
